hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18980","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn Ata, he said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Yamar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and a man asked him about Hajj at Arafah, and he said: Hajj is the day of Arafah, or Arafat, and whoever reaches the night of Jam before the Fajr prayer, his Hajj is complete. The days of Mina are three, so whoever hastens in two days, there is no sin on him, and whoever delays, there is no sin on him."
"18981","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn Ata al-Laythi, he said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Yamar al-Dayli saying: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while standing at Arafah, and some people of Najd came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, how is Hajj He said: Hajj is Arafah, so whoever comes before the Fajr prayer of the night of Jam, his Hajj is complete. The days of Mina are three days, so whoever hastens in two days, there is no sin on him, and whoever delays, there is no sin on him. Then he mounted a man behind him who began calling out with them."
"18982","Rawh narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn Ata al-Laythi, he said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Yamar al-Dayli, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying, and a man asked him about Hajj, and he said: Hajj is the day of Arafat, or Arafah, whoever reaches the night of Jam before praying the Fajr has reached Hajj. The days of Mina are three days, so whoever hastens in two days, there is no sin on him, and whoever delays, there is no sin on him."
